9T16:54:35Z"},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-03-06T22:58:46Z","updated_at":"2026-03-12T14:13:35Z","closed_at":"2026-03-12T14:13:35Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in v4.7.dev2.official 778cf54da\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev2 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Single-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-9400F CPU @ 2.90GHz (6 threads) - 47.93 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen running this script in any project:\n```gdscript\nextends Node\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tawait get_tree().process_frame\n\tvar a: Dictionary\n\tawait get_tree().process_frame\n```\n\nThe second of the two `await get_tree().process_frame` statements, and any subsequent instances of that statement in the block, prints this error when executed:\n```\nE 0:00:00:660   _unref: Parameter \"_p\" is null.\n  <C++ Source>  core/variant/dictionary.cpp:356 @ _unref()\n```\n\nThis issue also occurs if both await statements come immediately after the `var a: Dictionary` declaration:\n```gdscript\nextends Node\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tvar a: Dictionary\n\tawait get_tree().process_frame\n\tawait get_tree().process_frame\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUnzip, open, and run the attached MRP. Alternatively, create a node in any existing scene, attach a new script file to that node, paste in the above code, then save and run the scene.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[a-1.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25806066/a-1.zip)\n\nThe project contains a single main scene, whose root and only node has one of the above scripts attached to it.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"